WEBVTT

00:09.843 --> 00:11.469
[theme music]

00:30.071 --> 00:31.781
[suspenseful music]

00:31.865 --> 00:32.782
[growling]

00:33.450 --> 00:35.952
[Joon-seong whimpering]
Stay back, stay back.

00:36.036 --> 00:37.662
Stay away!

00:37.746 --> 00:39.372
No way we're going to heaven now.

00:40.248 --> 00:42.125
We're alive, so this is heaven.

00:42.751 --> 00:43.585
[yelps]

00:48.465 --> 00:50.717
[upbeat music]

00:55.472 --> 00:56.681
[zombie growling]

00:59.601 --> 01:00.810
2ND GRADE 5 CLASS

01:00.894 --> 01:02.145
[zombie growling]

01:07.150 --> 01:08.151
[growls]

01:10.403 --> 01:11.529
JUNG YONG-HYEON

01:15.283 --> 01:17.285
[thudding]

01:21.831 --> 01:23.083
I heard that in some countries,

01:23.166 --> 01:25.627
they mourn adults
more than they do with children.

01:25.710 --> 01:27.212
[somber music]

01:27.295 --> 01:29.672
[Nam-ra] And in others,
children more than adults.

01:31.216 --> 01:32.926
Which do you think our country is?

01:36.638 --> 01:37.764
What do you mean?

01:39.557 --> 01:42.644
When kids die, you lose hope but…

01:43.186 --> 01:45.730
when adults die, you lose their wisdom.

01:45.814 --> 01:47.899
-[Joon-yeong] Hope and wisdom.
-[helicopter whirring in distance]

01:47.982 --> 01:49.275
Which do we value more?

01:52.737 --> 01:53.738
Hmm?

01:56.324 --> 01:57.617
[helicopter whirring in distance]

01:58.368 --> 02:00.829
[Nam-ra] They've been flying
all over the place since yesterday.

02:01.830 --> 02:04.082
They would have already saved us
if they really wanted to.

02:07.293 --> 02:10.255
But even if they do come to save us,
we won't get out first.

02:12.465 --> 02:14.551
We're just not important enough for that.

02:14.634 --> 02:16.636
[somber music]

02:19.305 --> 02:21.349
We're students. That's it.

02:21.933 --> 02:23.726
[helicopter whirring in distance]

02:29.357 --> 02:30.775
[helicopter pilot] We're coming in.

02:30.859 --> 02:33.278
Set to control, steady.
Prepare for landing.

02:34.154 --> 02:35.738
Okay, roger.

02:37.657 --> 02:40.618
[helicopter pilot] Landing pad is clear.
We're touching down.

02:41.911 --> 02:44.414
RESCUE HEADQUARTERS

02:44.497 --> 02:46.166
[whirring]

02:48.251 --> 02:49.711
[helicopter whirring]

02:49.794 --> 02:51.838
[ominous music]

02:55.967 --> 02:59.053
We have everyone on board.
Heading to the quarantine camp now.

03:02.432 --> 03:05.018
[whooshing]

03:10.773 --> 03:12.483
[anchorman] Around 11:00 a.m.
this morning,

03:12.567 --> 03:15.028
the government announced
the declaration of martial law

03:15.111 --> 03:17.280
in an effort to control
the crisis in Hyosan.

03:17.780 --> 03:21.492
Starting sometime yesterday afternoon,
a strange epidemic began to spread,

03:21.576 --> 03:22.577
which lead to an evacuation order

03:22.660 --> 03:24.329
-and a city-wide lockdown.
-And a city-wide lockdown.

03:24.412 --> 03:28.625
It's the first time in 41 years
that martial law has been declared.

03:28.708 --> 03:30.877
[anchorwoman 1] Last time was
the Democratization Movement

03:30.960 --> 03:32.795
on May 18th, 1980.

03:32.879 --> 03:36.549
I repeat. Martial law has been declared
in order to control the Hyosan--

03:36.633 --> 03:39.260
[anchorwoman 2] The sense of panic
caused by the Hyosan epidemic

03:39.344 --> 03:41.554
has sent markets into a death spiral.

03:41.638 --> 03:44.682
Sidecar investments were activated
for both KOSPI and KOSDAQ

03:44.766 --> 03:46.684
which came as volatile
market respondent to Covid-19…

03:46.768 --> 03:49.604
[male protester] No refugees from Hyosan!
We don't want them!

03:49.687 --> 03:52.649
[protesters] We don't want them!
We don't want them!

03:52.732 --> 03:56.736
[male protester] No refugees. Go back!
Go back where you came from.

03:56.819 --> 04:00.406
[preacher] We are the Lord's people
who receives salvation.

04:00.990 --> 04:02.325
People will die as people,

04:02.408 --> 04:05.286
and demons are going to perish
as all demons must.

04:05.370 --> 04:06.621
[members] Amen.

04:07.205 --> 04:08.456
Get away!
[screaming]

04:08.539 --> 04:09.874
-Look out!
-[zombie growling]

04:10.792 --> 04:11.709
[screaming]

04:11.793 --> 04:12.961
[crowd clamoring]

04:13.044 --> 04:14.629
[male protester] You're killing us.

04:14.712 --> 04:16.547
[protesters] Go home!

04:16.631 --> 04:19.092
Come on, Zuki. It's okay, okay. Thank you.

04:19.676 --> 04:21.636
-Why won't you let us in?
-Get the hell of me.

04:22.220 --> 04:26.307
-[protesters] Send them back. Go home!
-[tense music]

04:26.391 --> 04:29.060
-Please. You have to help us!
-[protesters shouting indistinctly]

04:32.105 --> 04:33.398
REMOVE THE GOVERNMENT!

04:34.857 --> 04:36.484
[preacher] Our Lord Jesus Christ

04:36.567 --> 04:40.196
will not ask whether you are his son
or the son of the Devil.

04:40.280 --> 04:41.322
No. He won't.

04:44.158 --> 04:44.993
EVERYONE WILL DIE!

04:45.785 --> 04:47.996
[preacher] A person
who does not act righteously.

04:48.079 --> 04:51.165
A person who does not love
their brothers and sisters…

04:51.791 --> 04:53.084
REMOVE THE GOVERNMENT!

04:53.167 --> 04:55.086
…that is not one of God's people.

04:55.169 --> 04:56.170
[all] Amen!

04:56.254 --> 04:57.755
[all] Amen!

05:00.341 --> 05:03.177
-We're so gonna break a million views.
-[all laugh]

05:03.261 --> 05:04.846
[crowd clamoring]

05:09.267 --> 05:11.561
[anchorwoman 1]
A false rumor recently surfaced

05:11.644 --> 05:14.188
claiming that Hyosan epidemic
has spread to Seoul,

05:14.689 --> 05:18.151
as a result, the number of people
leaving Korea through Incheon Airport

05:18.234 --> 05:20.278
-rose to 228,000 in a day.
-[YouTuber] Hi, everyone. I apologize

05:20.361 --> 05:23.656
to the people, to all the viewers
we scared with our zombie skit

05:23.740 --> 05:25.616
we did on the subway.
[sucks teeth]

05:25.700 --> 05:28.328
Today, I'm on my knees
begging for your forgiveness…

05:28.411 --> 05:29.245
[inhales]

05:29.329 --> 05:33.041
…for accidentally misleading everyone
about the crisis in Hyosan…

05:33.124 --> 05:36.336
Is this what you expected? Really? Really?
[laughs]

05:36.419 --> 05:40.631
SUBWAY ZOMBIE PERFORMANCE
APOLOGY VIDEO

05:41.299 --> 05:44.594
[prime minister] We have to expand
martial law to control the media.

05:45.094 --> 05:49.390
There are rumors that radiation
from US nuclear bombs created the zombies.

05:49.474 --> 05:53.519
That the heads of Korea's
top 30 corporations fled the country.

05:53.603 --> 05:55.438
Most of the media are spreading fake news

05:55.521 --> 05:58.232
and sharing it online
without verifying sources.

05:58.316 --> 06:00.026
It's contributing to all the chaos.

06:00.109 --> 06:02.236
The government
should not control the media.

06:02.320 --> 06:05.073
The people themselves
should control the media.

06:05.156 --> 06:07.909
And our citizens
have enough power to do that.

06:07.992 --> 06:09.911
No expansion in martial law.

06:10.536 --> 06:12.205
[prime minister]
Let's focus on containment

06:12.288 --> 06:14.248
and rescuing the uninfected.

06:14.874 --> 06:16.375
Those are our priorities.

06:17.418 --> 06:19.045
-[Dae-su] Su-hyeok.
-[Wu-jin] Hey, Bare-su.

06:19.128 --> 06:21.005
-[panting]
-Are you okay?

06:21.089 --> 06:22.006
Where's the phone?

06:22.090 --> 06:23.132
And Cheong-san?

06:25.802 --> 06:27.053
[breathes nervously]

06:33.184 --> 06:34.352
[On-jo] Su-hyeok.

06:37.188 --> 06:38.397
Where is he?

06:38.481 --> 06:40.858
[suspenseful music]

06:43.194 --> 06:45.071
We got separated in the teacher's office.

06:46.322 --> 06:47.949
I'm sure he'll be fine.

06:48.032 --> 06:51.202
Are you serious? Oh, shit!

06:52.995 --> 06:54.038
I'm sorry…

06:55.456 --> 06:56.791
for coming back alone.

06:59.794 --> 07:00.670
[sighs]

07:03.714 --> 07:05.133
[grunts]

07:07.760 --> 07:08.886
-[growls]
-[groans]

07:10.429 --> 07:11.597
Come here.

07:12.306 --> 07:13.516
[Gwi-nam] Come here.

07:14.392 --> 07:16.853
[tense suspenseful music]

07:16.936 --> 07:18.521
[growling]

07:20.773 --> 07:21.774
[grunts]

07:23.734 --> 07:25.027
[grunting]

07:26.863 --> 07:28.614
Were you bit? You were bit, right?

07:28.698 --> 07:29.949
No, I--
[gasps]

07:30.825 --> 07:32.326
[groans]

07:36.831 --> 07:38.666
[whimpers, screams]

07:38.749 --> 07:40.460
-[growling]
-[screaming]

07:40.543 --> 07:43.045
[tense music]

07:50.678 --> 07:52.263
[growls]

07:52.346 --> 07:53.556
[grunts]

07:55.766 --> 07:56.934
-[grunts]
-[growling]

07:58.769 --> 08:00.188
[breathes angrily]

08:04.317 --> 08:05.651
[grunting]

08:07.987 --> 08:12.241
[snarling]

08:15.620 --> 08:16.996
[growls]

08:24.086 --> 08:24.921
[pants]

08:25.671 --> 08:26.506
[Gwi-nam grunts]

08:27.924 --> 08:29.383
[both panting]

08:30.426 --> 08:31.719
Cut it out.

08:32.678 --> 08:33.596
Give me the fucking phone.

08:33.679 --> 08:35.264
You killed the principal.
You're a murderer.

08:35.848 --> 08:36.974
You made me kill him. You shit.

08:38.017 --> 08:40.603
-You wanted proof I wasn't a coward.
-You're insane.

08:43.731 --> 08:45.149
[tense action music]

08:46.150 --> 08:47.276
[Gwi-nam grunts]

08:47.360 --> 08:48.486
-[grunts]
-[groans]

08:50.363 --> 08:51.447
[growls]

08:52.907 --> 08:53.866
-[growls]
-[groans]

08:54.408 --> 08:55.868
[growling]

08:59.455 --> 09:00.456
[both grunting]

09:06.212 --> 09:07.129
[zombies growling]

09:07.964 --> 09:09.131
[Gwi-nam] Get off me.

09:12.760 --> 09:14.762
-[grunts]
-[shatters]

09:18.516 --> 09:20.184
[growling]

09:20.268 --> 09:21.352
Should I save you?

09:22.144 --> 09:23.688
-[Cheong-san grunting]
-What do you say?

09:24.897 --> 09:26.148
[Cheong-san grunting]

09:26.232 --> 09:27.692
Beg for your life. Come on.

09:27.775 --> 09:29.151
Screw you.

09:30.319 --> 09:31.195
[grunts]

09:39.954 --> 09:41.163
[Gwi-nam gasps]

09:42.123 --> 09:43.666
[breathing heavily]

09:45.167 --> 09:46.502
[grunting]

09:47.086 --> 09:48.254
[Cheong-san whimpering]

09:53.259 --> 09:54.927
-[thuds]
-[Gwi-nam grunts]

09:55.428 --> 09:57.972
[screaming]

09:58.472 --> 09:59.890
[breathing heavily]

10:01.934 --> 10:03.561
-[Gwi-nam groans]
-[growling]

10:05.146 --> 10:07.565
[Gwi-nam screams]

10:08.149 --> 10:10.026
-[grunting]
-[growling]

10:10.818 --> 10:12.320
[zombies snarling]

10:13.070 --> 10:14.322
Damn it.

10:14.405 --> 10:15.740
Shit! Help me!

10:15.823 --> 10:17.074
[growling, munching]

10:17.158 --> 10:18.409
Cheong-san!

10:18.492 --> 10:19.577
[Gwi-nam] Cheong-san!

10:19.660 --> 10:20.745
Fuck!

10:22.413 --> 10:23.456
Oh, please!

10:24.415 --> 10:26.167
[whimpering]

10:29.253 --> 10:31.339
-[screaming]
-[growling, munching]

10:35.718 --> 10:37.011
[zombies munching]

10:39.013 --> 10:41.724
-[ominous music]
-I'll kill you.

10:41.807 --> 10:43.184
I will kill you.

10:43.851 --> 10:46.145
Fuck you.
[breathing heavily]

10:46.228 --> 10:47.146
I'll…

10:47.938 --> 10:49.315
I'll kill you.

10:49.899 --> 10:53.319
-[banging]
-[glass shattering]

11:03.788 --> 11:05.039
-[shudders]
-[banging continues]

11:05.706 --> 11:07.041
[whimpers]

11:09.293 --> 11:10.127
[sniffles, sobs]

11:10.961 --> 11:12.588
[munch, growl]

11:22.348 --> 11:23.724
[breathes heavily]

11:23.808 --> 11:26.894
[tense music]

11:29.021 --> 11:30.564
[Cheong-san grunts]

11:40.533 --> 11:41.951
[panting, grunting]

11:42.993 --> 11:45.204
Whoa!
[grunts]

11:58.509 --> 11:59.885
[snarls]

12:03.222 --> 12:05.057
-[grunting]
-[wood creaks]

12:07.059 --> 12:08.269
[growling]

12:10.146 --> 12:12.440
[zombies growling]

12:16.861 --> 12:18.154
[zombies snarling]

12:18.821 --> 12:20.781
[growls]

12:20.865 --> 12:22.283
[tense music]

12:22.950 --> 12:24.368
[Cheong-san grunting]

12:26.328 --> 12:27.663
[zombie snarls]

12:27.746 --> 12:28.998
[grunts]

12:31.041 --> 12:31.876
[growls]

12:32.918 --> 12:34.628
[panting, grunting]

12:34.712 --> 12:35.754
[growls]

12:39.925 --> 12:42.887
[tense music continues]

12:46.515 --> 12:48.267
[panting]

12:50.102 --> 12:51.896
[growling]

12:51.979 --> 12:54.064
[thudding]

12:57.818 --> 12:58.944
[snarling]

13:02.823 --> 13:04.033
[growling]

13:06.494 --> 13:07.328
[grunting]

13:09.121 --> 13:10.289
[grunts]

13:12.416 --> 13:14.084
-[grunting]
-[growling]

13:16.295 --> 13:17.338
[grunts]

13:19.965 --> 13:21.675
[panting]

13:22.259 --> 13:23.886
[Mi-jin breathes heavily]

13:24.720 --> 13:25.971
[sighs]
Shit.

13:26.472 --> 13:28.557
None of them are normal. All infected.

13:28.641 --> 13:30.768
-[zombie growling]
-Hey! He's coming!

13:30.851 --> 13:32.728
[Mi-jin] Oh, Shit. Shoot, shoot!

13:35.689 --> 13:36.690
[sighs in relief]
Oh, shit.

13:37.608 --> 13:39.818
We're gonna die
before we ever find your brother.

13:39.902 --> 13:40.986
[clattering]

13:44.532 --> 13:45.449
[sighs]

13:45.533 --> 13:46.575
Let's go, okay?

13:46.659 --> 13:48.827
[suspenseful music]

13:51.038 --> 13:53.332
[breathes heavily]

13:56.377 --> 13:57.670
Oh, shit.

13:59.004 --> 14:00.673
[whimpers]
Oh, seriously--

14:00.756 --> 14:01.966
[door closes]

14:04.635 --> 14:06.011
[glass shatters]

14:09.598 --> 14:12.059
[foreboding music]

14:13.227 --> 14:15.563
[breathes nervously]

14:23.654 --> 14:24.822
[breathes nervously]

14:24.905 --> 14:25.990
[tense music builds]

14:26.907 --> 14:27.741
[Mi-jin] Shit.

14:27.825 --> 14:29.618
[both sigh in relief]

14:29.702 --> 14:30.870
[sighs]

14:30.953 --> 14:33.539
I told you we should just
stay put, didn't I?

14:34.331 --> 14:36.625
How are we gonna find your brother
in the middle of all this?

14:36.709 --> 14:38.335
And it was just as crazy
to have come with her.

14:38.419 --> 14:39.503
-I told you--
-Hey. Hey!

14:39.587 --> 14:40.838
-[Mi-jin] What?
-There's a computer.

14:40.921 --> 14:42.214
[Mi-jin] Oh, yeah. Turn it on.

14:42.798 --> 14:44.884
Post on Instagram or Facebook for help.

14:44.967 --> 14:46.218
[Mi-jin sighs]
Oh, shit.

14:47.803 --> 14:49.221
-[computer chimes]
-[sighs]

14:49.305 --> 14:52.182
ADMIN

14:52.266 --> 14:53.851
[growling]

14:57.146 --> 14:59.189
[thumping]

15:07.156 --> 15:10.492
[Seon-moon] Martial Law Command
has acted swiftly and thoroughly.

15:11.285 --> 15:13.954
We sealed off the entire Hyosan area

15:14.038 --> 15:17.541
to prevent the situation
from spreading to other regions.

15:18.250 --> 15:19.919
[gasps, breathes shakily]

15:20.586 --> 15:23.422
If you live outside the area
under martial law,

15:23.505 --> 15:26.008
please stay calm and return
to your normal lives.

15:26.634 --> 15:30.304
Currently, Martial Law Command
is doing its absolute best

15:30.387 --> 15:34.725
to quarantine those infected
and to rescue and protect

15:34.808 --> 15:37.353
those who are not.

15:37.436 --> 15:38.354
EMERGENCY CALL

15:38.437 --> 15:43.067
We continue to operate, as always,
in strict compliance with the law

15:43.150 --> 15:44.401
and Federal regulations.

15:44.485 --> 15:45.903
EMERGENCY CALL
CONNECTING

15:46.570 --> 15:51.659
Fake news about the Hyosan epidemic
is spreading fast.

15:52.201 --> 15:54.078
Almost like a separate contagion.

15:54.662 --> 15:56.997
Martial Law Command will sensor

15:57.623 --> 16:01.710
all unconfirmed rumors, simultaneously,

16:02.419 --> 16:04.546
in the interest of operational efficiency,

16:05.214 --> 16:07.174
-all cell phone services…
-[phone line busy tone]

16:07.257 --> 16:08.968
…landlines, internet services,

16:09.051 --> 16:11.178
-and all communication originating…
-Why it isn't working?

16:11.261 --> 16:13.806
-…in Hyosan will be terminated…
-[Min-jae] Huh?

16:13.889 --> 16:15.099
What's wrong?

16:15.182 --> 16:17.393
-…from this point on.
-[reporters murmuring]

16:17.476 --> 16:19.853
-[camera shutters clicks]
-[indistinct chatter]

16:19.937 --> 16:21.397
[phone line busy tone]

16:24.024 --> 16:25.109
[clicking rapidly]

16:25.192 --> 16:27.444
That's so weird.
The internet cable's plugged in.

16:27.528 --> 16:29.071
-I'm trying to refresh it.
-Hey, get the phone over there.

16:29.154 --> 16:30.114
Okay.

16:32.741 --> 16:33.993
[beeping]

16:34.785 --> 16:35.995
[phone line busy tone]

16:36.078 --> 16:38.622
[sighs in annoyance]
Shit. Fucking assholes.

16:39.957 --> 16:41.750
They cut off the phones and internet.

16:41.834 --> 16:43.419
We at Martial Law Command,

16:43.502 --> 16:45.879
and its advisory council,
are doing our best

16:45.963 --> 16:47.506
to suppress the continuous spread.

16:48.757 --> 16:52.302
[Seon-moon] Moreover,
we are focusing all of our resources

16:53.053 --> 16:55.389
to rescue the people
who are currently trapped.

16:56.432 --> 16:59.977
If you live in Hyosan,
and you're watching this now,

17:00.853 --> 17:04.898
please try to stay hopeful and wait
in your location to be rescued.

17:04.982 --> 17:06.275
NO SIGNAL

17:06.358 --> 17:08.277
OCTOBER 21, THURSDAY

17:08.360 --> 17:10.487
[suspenseful music]

17:19.288 --> 17:20.164
[grunts]

17:22.583 --> 17:24.543
[breathing heavily]

17:28.464 --> 17:30.382
[gasps, breathes heavily]

17:31.800 --> 17:32.676
[phone chimes]

17:35.095 --> 17:36.680
[phone line busy tone]

17:37.765 --> 17:39.308
[grunting]

17:39.391 --> 17:41.518
[suspenseful music continues]

17:45.397 --> 17:46.523
[groans]

17:46.607 --> 17:47.483
[phone line busy tone]

17:47.566 --> 17:49.526
[screams frustratedly]

17:49.610 --> 17:52.029
[breathes angrily]

17:55.657 --> 17:57.034
[sobbing]

18:00.079 --> 18:02.456
[sobbing continues]

18:03.123 --> 18:05.209
WATER FLOW DETECTOR

18:06.627 --> 18:09.004
[growling]

18:11.673 --> 18:14.843
What do we do?
On-jo and Cheong-san are really close.

18:15.761 --> 18:17.137
[Ji-min] They're going out.

18:17.721 --> 18:19.098
But On-jo told me they're not.

18:20.307 --> 18:21.475
I'm telling you they are.

18:22.309 --> 18:23.727
[Ji-min] They're always together.

18:25.854 --> 18:27.147
[Hyo-ryeong] Really?

18:27.815 --> 18:29.358
NAM ON-JO

18:29.441 --> 18:30.734
Poor On-jo.

18:32.111 --> 18:33.320
[sighs deeply]

18:35.239 --> 18:37.825
[sentimental music]

18:42.454 --> 18:43.372
[sniffles]

18:44.081 --> 18:45.124
[sighs]

18:45.207 --> 18:48.085
I'm sure Cheong-san is fine.

18:49.920 --> 18:51.338
You know how fast he is.

18:53.048 --> 18:55.092
I don't know why he never listens.

18:55.801 --> 18:58.679
Ever since we were kids,
he's just never listened to me.

19:02.391 --> 19:04.685
I told him not to go,
but, of course, he did.

19:05.894 --> 19:06.979
I'm sorry.

19:08.939 --> 19:10.607
I should've brought him back here.

19:15.154 --> 19:16.238
[sighs]

19:16.780 --> 19:17.948
Where do you think…

19:21.076 --> 19:22.202
he is now?

19:24.621 --> 19:26.915
I'm pretty sure
he's in a safe hiding spot.

19:26.999 --> 19:28.750
[helicopter whirring in distance]

19:31.503 --> 19:33.755
[whirring]

19:39.136 --> 19:42.639
Joon-yeong. Didn't you mention
that your science club made a drone?

19:43.432 --> 19:46.143
Yeah. You want to look
for Cheong-san with it?

19:46.226 --> 19:49.605
-Could we?
-Well, yeah. But it's in the science lab.

19:49.688 --> 19:50.898
We can go get it.

19:50.981 --> 19:54.401
How would we get it?
It's crawling with zombies out there.

19:56.320 --> 19:57.404
That.

19:57.487 --> 20:00.157
[foreboding tense music]

20:00.240 --> 20:02.910
[Joon-yeong] You want me
to climb up on that?

20:02.993 --> 20:05.204
But there are zombies
in the science lab too.

20:05.287 --> 20:08.749
There weren't any
in the supply room. Right?

20:08.832 --> 20:10.042
That's true, but…

20:13.420 --> 20:15.130
We have to find Cheong-san.

20:16.506 --> 20:18.759
There's no one else besides us
to start looking

20:18.842 --> 20:20.302
and rescue people.

20:22.888 --> 20:23.889
[sighs]

20:26.308 --> 20:27.559
Yeah.

20:27.643 --> 20:29.478
It would be good if we had the drone.

20:29.561 --> 20:32.689
We can find Cheong-san and then
we can see how things are outside.

20:33.398 --> 20:36.735
[Nam-ra] We might even be able to send
an emergency message and ask for help.

20:36.818 --> 20:39.780
Sure, that would be really great.

20:41.615 --> 20:43.575
But who's gonna go?

20:43.659 --> 20:44.785
I wanna go.

20:45.702 --> 20:48.330
I took a fire rescue class,
and I've climbed ropes before.

20:49.665 --> 20:50.707
No, I'll go.

20:52.834 --> 20:54.336
You already went out there.

20:54.920 --> 20:57.089
[On-jo] You can't keep
putting yourself in danger.

20:57.172 --> 20:59.383
The drone isn't finished yet,

20:59.466 --> 21:01.218
we need to find
a few more parts to run it.

21:01.969 --> 21:03.553
Do you know what to get?

21:05.555 --> 21:07.391
[ominous music]

21:07.474 --> 21:08.308
[Joon-yeong sighs]

21:08.392 --> 21:10.060
Then I have to go anyway, I guess.

21:11.937 --> 21:12.980
I'll go with On-jo.

21:13.063 --> 21:14.106
No way.

21:18.068 --> 21:19.987
I'm actually going this time
so stand back.

21:20.070 --> 21:21.113
But you can't.

21:21.613 --> 21:23.365
He can't.
[chuckles]

21:23.448 --> 21:25.075
The rope won't hold you.

21:25.158 --> 21:29.288
It was fine when I came down.
But it'll snap if I climb up, right?

21:29.371 --> 21:31.832
-Yeah. Right.
-[Dae-su] Yeah. It'll snap.

21:31.915 --> 21:33.292
[Wu-jin] Right. Good boy.

21:34.084 --> 21:35.752
Joon-yeong, come with me.

21:37.296 --> 21:38.130
Mm.

21:40.966 --> 21:41.967
It's too dangerous.

21:42.968 --> 21:43.885
I'll go.

21:44.636 --> 21:45.637
[Joon-yeong groans]

21:53.562 --> 21:54.479
Thank you.

21:55.105 --> 21:56.356
But I don't want you…

21:58.066 --> 21:59.943
to be put in danger anymore.

22:02.612 --> 22:03.530
[Joon-yeong] I'm going.

22:05.782 --> 22:06.783
[groans]

22:11.496 --> 22:12.581
I'm going.

22:19.755 --> 22:20.797
[grunting]

22:21.590 --> 22:22.799
[breathes nervously]

22:32.309 --> 22:33.477
[Ji-min] Be careful, On-jo.

22:35.479 --> 22:38.315
Be safe. We'll be watching, okay?

22:38.398 --> 22:40.650
[suspenseful music]

22:49.534 --> 22:50.494
[grunts]

22:54.039 --> 22:56.333
[suspenseful music continues]

22:59.669 --> 23:00.712
[Hyo-ryeong] Do you think…

23:01.630 --> 23:03.215
it's really safe out there?

23:04.424 --> 23:05.383
I'm sure it is.

23:07.469 --> 23:09.888
Like you said,
there are soldiers and cops, right?

23:14.142 --> 23:17.312
I wanna go to my dad's factory
and my mom's sundae place.

23:18.480 --> 23:20.273
[snorts]
Whatever.

23:20.357 --> 23:22.567
You hate the smell
of leather and sundae anyway.

23:23.777 --> 23:25.362
[sniffles]
Yeah, I do.

23:26.071 --> 23:27.781
I just want my mom's sundae soup.

23:30.867 --> 23:31.910
[scoffs]

23:31.993 --> 23:34.996
So you finally grew up?
You should have said that earlier.

23:38.208 --> 23:39.417
Now, it's too late.

23:39.501 --> 23:40.335
[sighs]

23:41.169 --> 23:43.088
[zombie growling in distance]

23:44.297 --> 23:46.299
[quirky music]

23:46.383 --> 23:48.093
[Jae-ik] Hey. Hey, look.

23:49.344 --> 23:50.804
I bet there's a key in there, right?

23:52.556 --> 23:54.516
[sighs]
I don't think so.

23:56.977 --> 24:00.021
Shouldn't we just hide somewhere safe
and wait to be rescued?

24:00.105 --> 24:01.189
Hey.

24:01.273 --> 24:03.316
He said the solution
is on his laptop at the school.

24:03.400 --> 24:05.652
We have to hurry and notify
Fire and Disasters HQ.

24:06.403 --> 24:09.656
The people who have important information
need to survive, am I right?

24:09.739 --> 24:11.700
So doesn't our survival come first?

24:12.284 --> 24:13.618
Why do you keep acting
better than everyone

24:13.702 --> 24:16.288
like some elite leader of society?
You're from Seoul University?

24:17.497 --> 24:20.458
-Yeah.
-Huh? Wait?

24:21.084 --> 24:22.210
You really went there? Serious?

24:22.294 --> 24:25.088
Well, I haven't graduated yet.
I'm going back.

24:25.172 --> 24:26.381
Oh, grad school?

24:26.464 --> 24:28.550
-No. I'm a sophomore.
-What?

24:29.217 --> 24:32.053
Your exams? You retake?

24:32.137 --> 24:33.471
Uh, few times. Yeah.

24:34.389 --> 24:35.682
I went after high school.

24:37.726 --> 24:40.604
Oh, wow. I guess you must really
had your nose to the crime stuff, huh?

24:41.354 --> 24:42.480
Your face says it all.

24:43.773 --> 24:47.235
Hey. Apparently, you're smart,
so I'm gonna say this once.

24:48.028 --> 24:49.237
Be quiet and follow me.

24:49.946 --> 24:51.281
[splutters]
Wait.

24:51.364 --> 24:52.365
[grunts]

24:52.908 --> 24:53.742
Shit!

24:53.825 --> 24:54.784
[screams angrily]

24:55.869 --> 24:57.370
-[zombie growls]
-Whoa!

24:57.454 --> 24:58.288
[panting]

24:59.497 --> 25:00.874
[engine creaks]

25:00.957 --> 25:03.043
-[growls]
-[Jae-ik] Shut the door. Shut the door!

25:04.127 --> 25:05.295
-[growling]
-[grunting]

25:07.339 --> 25:08.757
Why won't it start?

25:08.840 --> 25:10.550
[screaming]

25:11.134 --> 25:12.302
[Ho-cheol] Hurry up!

25:12.385 --> 25:13.553
Please spare me!

25:14.179 --> 25:16.139
-[Jae-ik] Come on. This way.
-[Ho-cheol screaming]

25:16.223 --> 25:17.224
[Ho-cheol] Wait.

25:18.266 --> 25:20.268
-[Jae-ik] Let's go! Here.
-[bell chimes]

25:20.352 --> 25:21.353
Hurry!

25:21.436 --> 25:25.148
GOOD LUCK WITH YOUR NEW BUSINESS

25:25.232 --> 25:26.608
[growls]

25:26.691 --> 25:28.276
[Ho-cheol] Oh, my God.

25:29.236 --> 25:30.070
It's a zombie, sir.

25:30.153 --> 25:31.071
[growling]

25:31.154 --> 25:32.822
There's a zombie in here.

25:32.906 --> 25:34.783
[both panting]

25:37.869 --> 25:39.204
-[baby crying]
-[zombies growling]

25:40.288 --> 25:41.790
-In there?
-Yeah.

25:43.250 --> 25:44.084
Shit!

25:48.088 --> 25:49.297
[Hee-su growling]

25:49.381 --> 25:55.136
CHEONGSAN CHICKEN

25:55.220 --> 25:57.430
-It's all right. Come on.
-[zombie growling]

25:59.849 --> 26:00.684
Sure?

26:01.601 --> 26:03.144
She's tied up. it's okay.

26:05.855 --> 26:08.483
A student should be in school.
Why is she in a chicken place?

26:09.109 --> 26:09.943
And why she tied…

26:10.026 --> 26:11.027
Oh, my gosh!

26:12.195 --> 26:13.863
-What? What? What?
-[spluttering]

26:13.947 --> 26:15.115
Right there. There.

26:17.200 --> 26:19.202
What? What is that?

26:23.206 --> 26:24.916
Oh, shit.

26:30.046 --> 26:31.172
[Ho-cheol] Is… is it okay?

26:31.756 --> 26:33.383
Is, is the baby a zombie?

26:36.553 --> 26:38.471
No. It's alive.

26:38.555 --> 26:41.057
[growling]

26:45.645 --> 26:47.856
[somber music]

26:48.982 --> 26:51.151
[baby coos]

26:54.195 --> 26:55.739
[growls]

26:59.784 --> 27:02.120
Why don't you go check the fridge
for some milk or something?

27:02.203 --> 27:03.747
Why? Are you thirsty?

27:05.582 --> 27:06.666
It's for the baby.

27:07.876 --> 27:10.962
We need to feed this baby somehow.
It's very dehydrated.

27:13.965 --> 27:14.924
What if there's no milk?

27:15.508 --> 27:16.551
Can you just check first?

27:16.634 --> 27:18.678
Check the fridge,
and if there's no milk, come back,

27:18.762 --> 27:21.097
and we cross that bridge
when we come to it, okay?

27:21.181 --> 27:22.891
Uh, yeah. You're right. Yeah.

27:23.558 --> 27:27.270
-If there's no milk, maybe I should bring?
-Just check first. Can you do that?

27:28.480 --> 27:30.106
[Jae-ik] Check. Damn it.

27:30.190 --> 27:32.317
[croaking]

27:36.905 --> 27:37.947
What do we do now?

27:41.368 --> 27:44.371
What else can we do? Back to HQ.

27:46.247 --> 27:47.290
What about that?

27:48.750 --> 27:50.460
It's hard enough with just us.

27:50.543 --> 27:52.003
Are you gonna bring it along?

27:54.214 --> 27:55.924
[clanking]

27:59.677 --> 28:00.512
[chuckles]

28:03.890 --> 28:05.392
[panting]

28:06.935 --> 28:07.769
[grunts]

28:08.895 --> 28:09.896
Oh, careful.

28:10.855 --> 28:12.399
The drone and the bag are right there.

28:12.482 --> 28:14.526
[suspenseful music]

28:15.360 --> 28:16.444
[object clattering]

28:16.528 --> 28:17.487
[zipper zips]

28:17.570 --> 28:19.697
[Joon-yeong] Okay. Where was it?

28:21.116 --> 28:22.450
Where is the battery?

28:22.534 --> 28:23.410
[sniffles]

28:27.914 --> 28:28.915
[sighs]

28:30.041 --> 28:31.584
[objects clattering]

28:34.337 --> 28:36.506
[suspenseful music continues]

28:39.926 --> 28:42.011
I can't stop thinking
about this one thing.

28:42.846 --> 28:43.930
What?

28:48.476 --> 28:52.313
If eventually everyone in the world
but us ends up turning in too?

28:54.190 --> 28:55.150
No way.

28:56.443 --> 28:57.652
But if that were true?

28:59.237 --> 29:00.280
Nah.

29:01.865 --> 29:03.366
Then we'd be the minority.

29:04.659 --> 29:07.579
And all minorities
have a way of going extinct.

29:08.371 --> 29:09.289
[sighs]

29:11.499 --> 29:12.792
We're not the minority.

29:14.461 --> 29:16.129
But what if that actually happens?

29:17.714 --> 29:19.466
You think you could make it through this?

29:19.549 --> 29:21.551
[pensive music]

29:24.053 --> 29:25.054
I don't know.

29:27.474 --> 29:29.017
But I don't wanna be a zombie.

29:29.893 --> 29:31.436
[Su-hyeok] You don't recognize anyone.

29:32.228 --> 29:33.062
And…

29:35.940 --> 29:37.317
I won't even recognize you.

29:46.743 --> 29:49.162
In case I do get bitten,
I have a favor to ask.

29:50.872 --> 29:51.831
No.

29:52.874 --> 29:53.792
Don't get bit.

29:55.585 --> 29:57.420
-If by chance--
-No.

29:58.338 --> 29:59.714
Don't get bit. You can't.

30:01.299 --> 30:02.884
[Su-hyeok] Don't even think about dying.

30:05.470 --> 30:07.305
THIS DOOR DOES NOT OPEN FROM THE INSIDE

30:07.388 --> 30:08.890
Shit.

30:08.973 --> 30:11.017
[suspenseful music]

30:15.855 --> 30:16.731
[sighs]

30:19.818 --> 30:22.195
[breathes shakily]

30:23.363 --> 30:24.322
[metal clanks]

30:25.156 --> 30:25.990
[grunts]

30:30.620 --> 30:32.705
[suspenseful music continues]

30:34.916 --> 30:36.376
[metal clanks, creaks]

30:39.587 --> 30:41.923
-[grunting]
-[metal creaking]

30:42.006 --> 30:43.675
-[metal creaking]
-[grunts]

30:46.177 --> 30:47.011
[grunts]

30:47.929 --> 30:50.223
-[grunting]
-[metal creaking]

30:50.306 --> 30:52.183
[growls]

30:54.143 --> 30:55.103
[metal clanks]

30:56.813 --> 30:58.314
[growling]

30:58.898 --> 31:00.817
-[breathes heavily]
-[metal clanking]

31:03.653 --> 31:04.612
[metal clanks]

31:08.867 --> 31:10.785
-Eat up, I-sak.
-Thanks.

31:10.869 --> 31:13.830
[laughs]
On-jo. Which do you like better?

31:13.913 --> 31:17.292
-Mm, they're both good.
-Is that right?

31:17.375 --> 31:18.710
[laughs]

31:18.793 --> 31:20.795
[reflective music]

31:21.796 --> 31:23.756
-[breathes heavily]
-[metal clanking]

31:26.342 --> 31:28.219
Is it better like this?

31:29.220 --> 31:30.430
Or like this?

31:30.513 --> 31:32.473
[metal clanking]

31:36.936 --> 31:38.897
[laughing]

31:39.647 --> 31:40.857
Why?

31:40.940 --> 31:43.985
-[croaks]
-[laughter echoing]

31:45.111 --> 31:46.863
[whimpers]

31:47.697 --> 31:49.198
-[sniffles]
-[metal clanks]

31:51.576 --> 31:53.202
[breathes heavily]

31:56.414 --> 31:57.707
-[grunts]
-[growling]

31:57.790 --> 31:59.792
-[grunting]
-[metal clanking]

31:59.876 --> 32:01.419
[growls]

32:02.545 --> 32:04.631
-[groans]
-[tense music]

32:04.714 --> 32:05.548
-[grunts]
-[growling]

32:06.090 --> 32:08.593
Fuck this.
[screams angrily]

32:08.676 --> 32:10.511
[zombies growling]

32:10.595 --> 32:12.013
-[snarls]
-[panting]

32:12.847 --> 32:15.308
-[gasps]
-[growling]

32:15.808 --> 32:17.018
[loud thuds]

32:18.561 --> 32:20.188
[panting]

32:22.190 --> 32:23.024
[groans]

32:26.069 --> 32:27.111
-[growling]
-[grunts]

32:28.237 --> 32:29.364
MUSIC ROOM

32:35.912 --> 32:36.913
INSTRUMENT STORAGE

32:38.206 --> 32:39.248
[breathes heavily]

32:43.002 --> 32:44.128
[Joon-yeong] Hey, be careful.

32:44.629 --> 32:45.964
Take your time. Take your time.

32:47.173 --> 32:49.050
Come on. Come on. Come on. Come on.

32:49.133 --> 32:50.593
[breathes nervously]

32:56.891 --> 32:58.309
[breathes nervously]

32:59.811 --> 33:03.314
HELP, WE'RE IN THE BROADCASTING ROOM
IN HYOSAN HIGH SCHOOL

33:08.319 --> 33:09.862
[chimes]

33:09.946 --> 33:11.155
[drone chimes]

33:11.990 --> 33:13.032
Does it work?

33:13.616 --> 33:14.450
Is it working?

33:14.534 --> 33:15.618
I think it will.

33:16.661 --> 33:18.871
[pensive music]

33:21.290 --> 33:23.001
[drone whirring]

33:23.584 --> 33:24.502
Ooh.

33:28.339 --> 33:30.508
[whirring]

33:30.591 --> 33:31.509
[gasps]

33:31.592 --> 33:32.760
[Dae-su] Holy crap.

33:33.344 --> 33:34.595
That thing's crazy fast.

33:34.679 --> 33:37.348
I'll take it outside
after I find Cheong-san.

33:37.432 --> 33:39.892
If I find any rescuers out there,
I'll land in front of them.

33:39.976 --> 33:41.144
Okay. Okay, okay.

33:41.227 --> 33:43.021
[drone whirring]

33:43.688 --> 33:45.898
-Wait a second.
-[suspenseful music]

33:45.982 --> 33:48.401
They say when people know
their situation is hopeless,

33:50.111 --> 33:51.446
that's when they despair.

33:55.533 --> 33:56.659
Sweet saying.

33:57.744 --> 33:58.578
But what does that mean?

34:03.666 --> 34:06.711
Even if everyone in the world
but us turned into zombies,

34:07.670 --> 34:09.881
we can't fall in to despair.

34:09.964 --> 34:12.675
Ahh. So that's what that means?

34:14.427 --> 34:15.470
Nam-ra.

34:16.095 --> 34:18.598
It's best to make a plan
and try to stick to it,

34:19.432 --> 34:22.185
but we're not all top students,
and we can't be as smart as you.

34:23.603 --> 34:26.022
Being logical isn't part of human nature.

34:26.105 --> 34:27.940
In a crisis, it's better to be logical.

34:28.024 --> 34:29.609
We need hope more than logic.

34:31.319 --> 34:33.029
Don't you think that's best right now?

34:35.948 --> 34:37.950
Hey. I think…

34:38.826 --> 34:40.953
flying the drone
is what we need right now.

34:43.664 --> 34:45.458
-Okay. Try it.
-Here goes.

34:45.541 --> 34:47.335
-[Dae-su] Mm.
-[drone whirring]

34:48.086 --> 34:50.379
[tense music]

34:59.555 --> 35:01.557
[tense music continues]

35:10.024 --> 35:11.776
[gasps]
Oh, no.

35:12.527 --> 35:13.820
Everyone's zombie.

35:16.531 --> 35:17.782
[music fades]

35:20.785 --> 35:21.619
[sighs]

35:21.702 --> 35:23.788
I shouldn't even bother studying.

35:23.871 --> 35:24.705
Shit.

35:24.789 --> 35:26.290
I can't take my CSAT anyway.

35:27.166 --> 35:29.544
Shit. I'll never studying again
as long as I live.

35:30.294 --> 35:32.421
Can you please be serious
for once in your life?

35:32.505 --> 35:34.298
I'm dead serious right now.

35:35.842 --> 35:38.302
What are you gonna do?
Keep looking for your brother?

35:40.805 --> 35:42.807
The archery center has an emergency phone.

35:42.890 --> 35:45.017
It automatically connects
to emergency services.

35:45.101 --> 35:46.269
-Really?
-Yeah.

35:46.352 --> 35:48.729
We got a hotline installed a while ago
because of some injuries.

35:48.813 --> 35:51.858
And if it doesn't connect?
All the phones and internet are dead.

35:51.941 --> 35:53.025
It doesn't matter.

35:54.610 --> 35:56.404
That's where all the arrows are anyway.

35:57.196 --> 35:58.656
I have less than 20 left.

35:58.739 --> 36:01.033
We'll need more
if we wanna leave the school alive.

36:01.117 --> 36:03.119
-I think, uh--
-Okay, let's go.

36:03.911 --> 36:05.997
Go to the archery center
so we can get your arrows.

36:06.080 --> 36:09.250
Then we should probably go home
or maybe go to a supermarket.

36:09.834 --> 36:11.502
You know. In most zombie movies,

36:11.586 --> 36:14.672
the ones that go to supermarkets
always manage to survive in the end.

36:15.965 --> 36:17.133
And they have cigs.

36:17.216 --> 36:18.342
I think that we--

36:18.426 --> 36:20.469
[Min-jae] The dumpsters
are right under these windows.

36:21.512 --> 36:23.639
I think it's better to jump
than use the stairs.

36:24.432 --> 36:27.226
[sighs]
Yeah. Let's jump.

36:27.310 --> 36:30.104
Falling from the third floor is way better
than falling your exams, right?

36:31.147 --> 36:32.940
Hey, let me get a word in!

36:33.024 --> 36:33.941
Hey, Min-jae.

36:34.025 --> 36:36.235
Go down first and shoot any
that come running.

36:36.319 --> 36:37.653
[Min-jae] Okay.

36:37.737 --> 36:39.947
Then you two go down
and help him out as much as you can.

36:40.031 --> 36:41.782
I'll cover you out in the hallway
and bring up the rear.

36:41.866 --> 36:42.783
Mm.

36:43.951 --> 36:45.161
What do you wanna say?

36:45.244 --> 36:47.121
Uh, I think we should just stay here.

36:47.747 --> 36:50.041
The adults will rescue us.

36:50.791 --> 36:52.335
If you wanna stay, be my guest.

36:53.711 --> 36:55.046
But I don't trust adults.

36:59.634 --> 37:03.095
Ahh, shit. She's just so my type.

37:03.179 --> 37:05.348
[Joon-seong sighs]
I'm too scared to stay here alone.

37:06.265 --> 37:07.225
Hurry up.

37:11.771 --> 37:13.356
[suspenseful music]

37:13.439 --> 37:14.690
[zombies growling in distance]

37:17.193 --> 37:18.319
[zombie shrieks]

37:26.452 --> 37:27.536
[breathes heavily]

37:28.079 --> 37:29.413
[panting]

37:29.497 --> 37:31.540
[suspenseful music]

37:32.208 --> 37:33.417
[growling]

37:35.586 --> 37:36.712
[groans]

37:37.463 --> 37:39.757
-Look out! Behind you!
-[growls]

37:39.840 --> 37:40.967
Move.

37:43.302 --> 37:44.303
[shrieks]

37:44.387 --> 37:45.263
[gasps]

37:45.346 --> 37:46.514
[growling]

37:47.598 --> 37:48.474
[whimpers]

37:48.557 --> 37:50.977
Oh, shit. Why are we so high up?

37:53.229 --> 37:55.481
-Jump already.
-All right, I'm going.

37:56.649 --> 37:58.150
[screams]

37:59.318 --> 38:00.653
[groans]
Shit.

38:00.736 --> 38:01.570
[pants]

38:01.654 --> 38:02.989
[growling in distance]

38:09.829 --> 38:11.747
[growling]

38:12.873 --> 38:14.208
[drone whirring]

38:18.671 --> 38:20.047
No one in the infirmary.

38:20.840 --> 38:22.466
Joon-yeong, go somewhere else.

38:26.554 --> 38:28.139
Wait. Hold on. Stop right there.

38:28.931 --> 38:30.266
[Wu-jin] Is that an arrow?

38:30.349 --> 38:31.767
-Where?
-This.

38:32.685 --> 38:34.103
[Dae-su] You're right. It is.

38:34.186 --> 38:35.604
Why? What?

38:37.648 --> 38:38.649
My older sister.

38:40.735 --> 38:42.111
She had a competition today.

38:48.576 --> 38:49.869
[music fades]

38:54.457 --> 38:57.126
[dramatic music]

39:01.297 --> 39:03.049
Where the hell did Cheong-san go?

39:09.055 --> 39:10.598
[breathes heavily]

39:16.896 --> 39:19.023
[dramatic music continues]

39:30.326 --> 39:33.746
-[metal creaking]
-[thudding]

39:34.997 --> 39:36.332
[screeching]

39:39.377 --> 39:40.211
[drone whirring]

39:41.796 --> 39:43.297
It's Cheong-san!

39:43.381 --> 39:45.216
-What room is that?
-Cheong-san!

39:45.299 --> 39:46.342
He… He can't hear you.

39:46.425 --> 39:48.344
-[Wu-jin] Be quiet.
-[suspenseful music]

39:48.427 --> 39:50.679
-Hey, Cheong-san!
-He can't hear you.

39:50.763 --> 39:51.722
On-jo, it's okay.

39:51.806 --> 39:52.848
[gasps]

39:52.932 --> 39:54.350
Cheong-san is alive!

39:54.433 --> 39:55.976
[Su-hyeok] Cheong-san is alive!

39:56.060 --> 39:57.561
[breathes heavily]

40:02.650 --> 40:03.526
Ah…

40:06.779 --> 40:09.448
What's he doing? Where's he going?

40:09.532 --> 40:10.866
[Dae-su] Look this way! Over here!

40:10.950 --> 40:12.952
Where are you going, you stupid moron?

40:13.035 --> 40:14.161
He can't hear you, Dae-su!

40:14.245 --> 40:17.331
[Wu-jin] Be quiet, will you?
You're so damn loud.

40:17.415 --> 40:18.582
[Dae-su] My bad. My bad.

40:20.876 --> 40:22.670
-Didn't you say the battery was low?
-[Joon-yeong sighs]

40:22.753 --> 40:25.673
Yeah. I couldn't charge it,
so it's almost dead.

40:25.756 --> 40:27.925
Now that we know for sure
where Cheong-san is,

40:28.008 --> 40:29.760
let's go look somewhere else.

40:29.844 --> 40:31.720
You wanted to check outside
and ask for help?

40:32.680 --> 40:34.682
On-jo, is that okay?

40:35.850 --> 40:38.352
Mm-hmm. Now that we know he's alive.

40:39.061 --> 40:39.937
Okay. Here it goes.

40:42.898 --> 40:44.233
[drone whooshes, whirring]

40:48.612 --> 40:49.697
[Dae-su] Whoa.

40:49.780 --> 40:51.574
It's totally Zombieland out there.

40:52.908 --> 40:55.494
I think we should look
outside of the school grounds.

40:56.996 --> 40:58.205
Let's take it outside.

40:58.789 --> 40:59.665
Okay.

40:59.748 --> 41:01.792
[suspenseful music]

41:06.422 --> 41:07.548
[drone whirring]

41:11.093 --> 41:12.344
[zombies growling in distance]

41:13.220 --> 41:14.263
[Ji-min] Wait a minute.

41:14.889 --> 41:16.265
What is it?

41:16.348 --> 41:18.642
Wait a sec.
[breathes shakily]

41:18.726 --> 41:19.602
Just… wait.

41:20.227 --> 41:22.771
[Ji-min gasps, sobbing]

41:26.358 --> 41:27.818
-[sobbing]
-What?

41:31.363 --> 41:33.240
[Hyo-ryeong] Wha, what's wrong, Ji-min?

41:33.324 --> 41:34.950
Wait a minute.
[whimpering]

41:36.285 --> 41:39.330
I-I can't…
[sobbing]

41:41.874 --> 41:43.334
What? What is it?

41:44.168 --> 41:46.045
[Ji-min sobbing]

41:47.922 --> 41:48.839
This…

41:48.923 --> 41:51.467
-[whimpers]
-[somber music]

41:51.550 --> 41:53.761
That's my dad's car.
[whimpering]

41:55.971 --> 41:57.014
[Joon-yeong] Which one?

41:57.723 --> 41:59.600
The white one? The black one?

41:59.683 --> 42:02.186
[Ji-min cries]
It's this truck.

42:02.269 --> 42:03.103
[sobs]

42:03.187 --> 42:04.605
It's my dad's car.

42:06.357 --> 42:07.483
[whimpering]

42:09.068 --> 42:10.027
Don't worry.

42:10.861 --> 42:12.780
I'm sure there are lots of cars like that.

42:12.863 --> 42:14.323
[Ji-min crying]

42:14.406 --> 42:16.408
-Hang on. I'll check.
-[Ji-min whimpers]

42:24.708 --> 42:27.878
[wailing]

42:29.880 --> 42:30.714
[sighs]

42:32.424 --> 42:34.134
[Ji-min crying]

42:38.430 --> 42:40.474
[somber music continues]

42:47.189 --> 42:49.191
-Ji-min.
-[crying]

42:54.822 --> 42:56.782
[crying, breathes heavily]

43:00.077 --> 43:01.579
[growling]

43:01.662 --> 43:03.497
[drone beeping, chimes]

43:03.581 --> 43:05.916
[zombies snarling]

43:08.168 --> 43:10.129
[wind whooshing]

43:11.255 --> 43:12.923
[helicopter whirring]

43:15.384 --> 43:17.469
[ominous music]

43:19.138 --> 43:22.558
11:47 AM
ABANDONED PRISON IN THE SUBURB OF HYOSAN

43:23.225 --> 43:24.602
[helicopter whirring]

43:30.566 --> 43:32.234
[whirring continues]

43:40.868 --> 43:42.911
[ominous music continues]

43:51.337 --> 43:53.297
[whirring]

44:02.556 --> 44:06.185
[male announcer]
Attention, citizens of Hyosan.

44:06.268 --> 44:07.603
Please proceed calmly…

44:07.686 --> 44:10.939
-Where are we going? Where are we going?
-…to the first quarantine.

44:11.023 --> 44:13.359
-Do you see us--
-Don't you!

44:13.442 --> 44:14.276
-Hey!
-We're not animals!

44:14.360 --> 44:16.153
-We've been waiting here for hours!
-Please cooperate

44:16.236 --> 44:18.697
with the tests to determine
whether or not you are infected…

44:18.781 --> 44:19.698
[indistinct clamoring]

44:19.782 --> 44:23.786
…will be returned to you
at the later stage.

44:24.787 --> 44:26.121
I repeat.

44:27.289 --> 44:31.877
Please proceed calmly
to the first quarantine checkpoint…

44:31.960 --> 44:35.047
and surrender your personal belongings.

44:35.130 --> 44:40.177
This is for your safety,
and the safety of those around you.

44:40.761 --> 44:44.098
We appreciate your continuous cooperation.

44:45.474 --> 44:46.433
EXAMINATION ROOM

44:47.351 --> 44:50.562
Thank you for your service.
Where's the control room?

44:55.025 --> 44:56.193
As per Martial Law,

44:56.777 --> 44:58.987
you have to quarantine
until you are examined.

44:59.071 --> 45:01.448
Why in the world
would she have to quarantine now?

45:01.532 --> 45:02.825
She just came back from a battlefield--

45:02.908 --> 45:04.827
-It's okay. That's enough.
-Unbelievable.

45:05.994 --> 45:07.538
So, where is the control room?

45:07.621 --> 45:09.665
[soldier 1] You have to be examined first.

45:09.748 --> 45:11.917
I'm not refusing to be examined.

45:12.000 --> 45:13.919
[soldier 1] Please follow the protocols.

45:14.002 --> 45:17.339
Hyosan Fire Station.
Rescue Team One, Captain Nam So-ju.

45:17.423 --> 45:19.633
I was responsible for them
from mobilization until rescue.

45:19.716 --> 45:20.717
[soldier 1] Enough!

45:21.218 --> 45:23.053
Does it sound like
I'm asking your opinion?

45:24.304 --> 45:26.765
-[soldier 1] Take them to the exam room.
-[soldier 2] Yes, sir.

45:26.849 --> 45:28.892
[dramatic music]

45:41.447 --> 45:42.489
[Eun-hee] What is this place?

45:43.991 --> 45:45.492
This isn't an examination room.

45:46.160 --> 45:48.120
[soldier 2] There are lots
of people in line for exams,

45:48.203 --> 45:49.121
you have to wait your turn.

45:49.204 --> 45:52.291
Then you should've explained the situation
and asked her to wait somewhere else

45:52.374 --> 45:53.584
and then escorted her.

45:53.667 --> 45:55.377
What the hell is wrong with you?

45:55.461 --> 45:57.337
[soldier 2] There are plenty
of other people outside

45:57.421 --> 46:00.090
who are sitting on mats
on a concrete floor.

46:00.716 --> 46:02.759
We're trying to make you
as comfortable as possible

46:02.843 --> 46:04.136
because you're an assemblywoman.

46:05.929 --> 46:09.099
The wait time
for an examination is 12 to 72 hours.

46:10.017 --> 46:11.059
Wait a minute.

46:12.227 --> 46:13.979
My daughter is at her school right now.

46:14.605 --> 46:16.523
It may be too late if we keep waiting.

46:17.691 --> 46:18.984
Please request a rescue.

46:20.110 --> 46:21.820
[soldier 2] We're doing the best we can.

46:23.280 --> 46:24.198
Wait here for now.

46:25.824 --> 46:27.743
[clattering]

46:32.164 --> 46:34.333
[suspenseful music]

46:42.132 --> 46:44.218
[insect buzzing]

46:49.765 --> 46:52.392
[buzzing continues]

46:58.440 --> 47:00.067
[buzzing]

47:00.776 --> 47:02.319
[gasps]

47:02.402 --> 47:04.530
[foreboding music]

47:08.200 --> 47:09.326
[breathes]

47:10.536 --> 47:12.204
[gasping]

47:21.296 --> 47:22.923
Oh, shit.

47:24.341 --> 47:25.592
Did I die?

47:28.178 --> 47:29.805
Am I dead?

47:29.888 --> 47:30.764
[growling]

47:31.306 --> 47:32.599
[gasps]

47:37.354 --> 47:38.397
[flustered gasping]

47:38.480 --> 47:40.190
[growling]

47:42.442 --> 47:44.278
[Gwi-nam whimpering]

47:45.821 --> 47:47.322
[breathes heavily]

47:50.701 --> 47:51.785
Hey.

47:51.868 --> 47:52.911
-[growls]
-[gasps]

48:00.252 --> 48:03.046
Aren't, aren't you gonna eat me,
you zombie bastards?

48:03.130 --> 48:04.756
-[growling]
-[Gwi-nam whimpers]

48:06.383 --> 48:08.552
I gave them serotonin injections
for a week,

48:08.635 --> 48:10.596
but it had no effect whatsoever.

48:11.305 --> 48:13.765
The moment an antivirus enters the body,

48:13.849 --> 48:16.602
the virus mutates
and stops attacking its target.

48:17.352 --> 48:20.439
[Mr. Lee] The only explanation
is that the cells learn and evolve.

48:23.859 --> 48:25.110
If this virus…

48:26.695 --> 48:28.947
manages to learn human consciousness…

48:29.031 --> 48:30.574
-[thuds]
-[squelches]

48:40.667 --> 48:42.794
…a new species of humankind could be born.

48:44.463 --> 48:45.881
[thuds]

48:49.468 --> 48:50.802
[growls]

48:51.928 --> 48:53.722
Cheong-san, you son of a bitch!

48:55.015 --> 48:56.308
I'll kill you.

48:56.391 --> 48:58.018
[breathes heavily]

48:58.935 --> 49:00.687
[metal clanking]

49:03.273 --> 49:05.150
[metal clanking]

49:08.236 --> 49:10.322
[tense music]

49:11.990 --> 49:12.991
[screeching]

49:18.705 --> 49:20.832
[tense music continues]

49:23.418 --> 49:24.503
[screeches]

49:32.135 --> 49:33.428
[zombies growling in distance]

49:35.639 --> 49:36.807
[growling]

49:45.023 --> 49:46.900
What the fuck?
[sighs]

49:51.738 --> 49:52.864
That means…

49:55.701 --> 49:58.495
ONE HEART

49:58.578 --> 49:59.746
…I'm God.

50:07.504 --> 50:09.673
[screaming]
Hey, Cheong-san!

50:09.756 --> 50:11.299
[zombies growling]

50:20.142 --> 50:22.269
[closing theme music]

54:08.286 --> 54:11.998
ALL CHARACTERS, LOCATIONS, ORGANIZATIONS,
AND EVENTS IN THIS SHOW ARE FICTIONAL.
